  "summary": "Recent preprints and publications assign specific adaptors, tethers and condensates to distinct stress contexts in organelle quality control.",
  "synthesis": "The items share a focus on stress-responsive remodeling of organelles through selective autophagy, although they span different compartments and stress types. In preprints, Contact-phagy uses SIGMAR1-CCPG1 to turn over ER-mitochondria contact-site subdomains, and the yeast ER-vacuole tether Mdm1 supports starvation-induced autophagy by balancing phospholipid and neutral lipid metabolism to allow autophagosome completion. Published work links iron deficiency to pexophagy through a GABARAP-FLCN/FNIP1 interaction that activates TFEB and TFE3. Processing bodies form during recovery from lysosomal damage and collaborate with stress granules to support lysosomal quality and cell survival. RAB11 and RAB30 cooperate on endosomes under starvation, shear and osmotic stress, using phosphoinositide turnover to drive autophagy. What is new is the assignment of specific adaptors, tethers and condensates to each stress context.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-haiku-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-11-21"
}
